{"t": 229.76, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "sshi_zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR design fails due to efficiency losses (S2, S4) and lack of overvoltage protection (S3). I am implementing a Parallel-SSHI (Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor) topology to invert the piezoelectric capacitance voltage at each half-cycle, significantly increasing the harvested energy to meet vavg requirements. I've added a DZ33 Zener diode as a clamp on the output node to prevent vout from exceeding 3.6 V in high-excitation conditions (S3). A larger storage capacitor is used to suppress ripple and improve settling stability (S5).", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "sshi_zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR design fails due to efficiency losses (S2, S4) and lack of overvoltage protection (S3). I am implementing a Parallel-SSHI (Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor) topology to invert the piezoelectric capacitance voltage at each half-cycle, significantly increasing the harvested energy to meet vavg requirements. I've added a DZ33 Zener diode as a clamp on the output node to prevent vout from exceeding 3.6 V in high-excitation conditions (S3). A larger storage capacitor is used to suppress ripple and improve settling stability (S5).", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "Cout", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 4.7e-06}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.0001}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 5e-06, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}]}}
